some random info:

You can type these into Win + R, Command Prompt, PowerShell, or a Start-menu search. .msc files open Microsoft Management Console tools; .cpl files open classic Control Panel applets. Microsoft documents the general control <applet> approach, though some legacy items have been replaced or redirected by Windows 11 Settings.

Most useful .msc consoles
Run command	Opens	Useful for
compmgmt.msc	Computer Management	One console containing Event Viewer, Task Scheduler, Device Manager, Disk Management, Services, Shared Folders, etc.
devmgmt.msc	Device Manager	Drivers, devices, USB/audio/MIDI hardware, hidden devices
diskmgmt.msc	Disk Management	Partitions, drive letters, VHDs, volumes
eventvwr.msc	Event Viewer	System/app logs, crashes, driver events, service failures
services.msc	Services	Start/stop/configure Windows and third-party services
taskschd.msc	Task Scheduler	Scheduled tasks, startup automation, triggers
perfmon.msc	Performance Monitor	Counters, Data Collector Sets, performance logs
resmon	Resource Monitor	Per-process CPU, disk, network, memory activity
msinfo32	System Information	Hardware, drivers, Secure Boot, BIOS, loaded modules
msconfig	System Configuration	Boot options and diagnostic startup
gpedit.msc	Local Group Policy Editor	Local policy settings; normally Pro/Enterprise/Education, not Home
secpol.msc	Local Security Policy	Security policy, audit policy, user-right assignment; usually Pro+
lusrmgr.msc	Local Users and Groups	Local accounts/groups; normally Pro+
certmgr.msc	Certificates — Current User	Inspect/import/export user certificates
certlm.msc	Certificates — Local Computer	Machine certificate stores; run elevated when needed
wf.msc	Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security	Inbound/outbound firewall rules and connection security
gpresult /h "%USERPROFILE%\Desktop\gpresult.html"	Group Policy report	Generates an HTML report of applied policy
rsop.msc	Resultant Set of Policy	GUI view of effective policy settings; availability can vary
fsmgmt.msc	Shared Folders	SMB shares, open files, connected users
printmanagement.msc	Print Management	Printers, drivers, ports; normally Pro+
comexp.msc	Component Services	COM+, DCOM permissions/configuration
dcomcnfg	Component Services / DCOM config	Same management area as Component Services
wmimgmt.msc	WMI Control	WMI repository status and security
secpol.msc	Local Security Policy	Security options, auditing, user rights
azman.msc	Authorization Manager	Legacy authorization tool; may not be installed/usable
tpm.msc	TPM Management	TPM readiness, status, ownership information
devmgmt.msc	Device Manager	Device power management and driver troubleshooting
optionalfeatures	Windows Features	Enable/disable .NET, Hyper-V components, SMB, WSL-related features
napclcfg.msc	NAP Client Configuration	Obsolete on current Windows; usually not useful
compmgmt.msc, devmgmt.msc, diskmgmt.msc, eventvwr.msc, services.msc, and taskschd.msc are the main everyday administrative consoles. Some, including Group Policy and Local Users and Groups, are unavailable in standard Windows Home editions.

