Audio, MIDI, and device shortcuts
Since you work with audio devices and MIDI, these are particularly useful:

text
mmsys.cpl
control mmsys.cpl,,0
control mmsys.cpl,,1
control mmsys.cpl,,3
joy.cpl
devmgmt.msc
ms-settings:apps-volume
ms-settings:sound
ms-settings:privacy-microphone
A compact troubleshooting sequence:

text
1. mmsys.cpl                 → confirm default playback/recording device
2. control mmsys.cpl,,1      → inspect mic/interface inputs
3. ms-settings:apps-volume   → check per-app output routing and volume
4. devmgmt.msc               → verify USB interface/driver state
5. eventvwr.msc              → inspect audio-driver or USB disconnect events
6. resmon                    → check whether a process is pegging CPU/disk
Build your own MMC toolbox
Run:

text
mmc
Then choose:

text
File → Add/Remove Snap-in
Useful snap-ins to combine into a saved personal .msc file:

Event Viewer

Device Manager

Disk Management

Services

Task Scheduler

Performance Monitor

Local Users and Groups

Certificates — Current User / Local Computer

Shared Folders

Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security

WMI Control
Save it somewhere convenient, for example as a custom Dev Diagnostics.msc. MMC is the host framework for these snap-ins, and .msc consoles are launchable/savable management-console files.
